  tooltipConfigs:
  - title: Lock Windows
    message: Locks all window movement and scaling
    footer: Main menu
    icon: {fileID: 0}
  - title: Settings Window
    message: Load skins and bundles or configure keybinds
    footer: Main menu
    icon: {fileID: 0}
  - title: File Window
    message: Load and save files or create a new map
    footer: Main menu
    icon: {fileID: 0}
  - title: Asset Hierarchy
    message: Add prefabs, collections, and monuments to your scene
    footer: Main menu
    icon: {fileID: 0}
  - title: Items List
    message: Locate and modify prefabs, collections, monuments, and paths in your
      scene
    footer: Main menu
    icon: {fileID: 0}
  - title: Terrain Painter
    message: Modify map layers and heightmap, and configure monuments for export
    footer: Main menu
    icon: {fileID: 0}
  - title: Geology Window
    message: Customize prefab generation across the map
    footer: Main Menu
    icon: {fileID: 0}
  - title: Prefab Breaker
    message: Inspect assets and assign prefabs to build "broken" monuments
    footer: Main menu
    icon: {fileID: 0}
  - title: Paths Tool
    message: Select, modify, or create paths
    footer: Main menu
    icon: {fileID: 0}
  - title: Console
    message: Command line interface with logging. Type /help to get started
    footer: Main menu
    icon: {fileID: 0}
  - title: About
    message: Information about RustMapper
    footer: Main Menu
    icon: {fileID: 0}
  - title: Scale / Exit
    message: Set default window sizes or Exit RustMapper
    footer: Main menu
    icon: {fileID: 0}
  - title: Compass
    message: Shows location vector, map grid, and camera direction. Entering coordinates
      will move the camera.
    footer: 
    icon: {fileID: 0}
  - title: Height map
    message: Brushes modify the height of the terrain
    footer: Terrain Type
    icon: {fileID: 0}
  - title: Water map
    message: Brushes modify the height of an invisible watermap which controls water
      effects only
    footer: Terrain Type
    icon: {fileID: 0}
  - title: Holes map
    message: Brushes create or remove holes in the terrain. This ONLY modifies terrain
      visibility.
    footer: Terrain type
    icon: {fileID: 0}
  - title: Splat map
    message: Brushes change the terrain's texture and appearance
    footer: Terrain type
    icon: {fileID: 0}
  - title: Biome map
    message: Brushes change the environment
    footer: Terrain type
    icon: {fileID: 0}
  - title: Topology maps
    message: These many layers interact with Rust's resource and player spawners.
      'Ocean' places water
    footer: Terrain Type
    icon: {fileID: 0}
  - title: Monument map
    message: Brushes create the map which blends monuments into map terrains. Toggles
      define which terrain layers are used.
    footer: Monument Editor
    icon: {fileID: 0}
  - title: Category
    message: Identifies Dungeons and defines Monument Markers
    footer: Inspector
    icon: {fileID: 0}
  - title: Find in Breaker
    message: Locate itembs built by the Prefab Breaker
    footer: Inspector
    icon: {fileID: 0}
  - title: Save Collection
    message: All selected prefabs will be saved as a .prefab file with filename defined
      by Category
    footer: Inspector
    icon: {fileID: 0}
  - title: ID Field
    message: IDs are unique hash integers for internal use
    footer: Inspector
    icon: {fileID: 0}
  - title: Prefab Controls
    message: Holding shift while using gizmos fixes changes to Snap values
    footer: Inspector
    icon: {fileID: 0}
  - title: Items Search
    message: When a query is entered, the list only shows matching items
    footer: Items Window
    icon: {fileID: 0}
  - title: Delete Selection
    message: Removes all checked prefabs from scene
    footer: Items Window
    icon: {fileID: 0}
  - title: Unselect All
    message: Unchecks all items in search query
    footer: Items Window
    icon: {fileID: 0}
  - title: Select All
    message: Checks all items in search query
    footer: Items Window
    icon: {fileID: 0}
  - title: Search Field
    message: Only assets matching the Query and their parent folders will be shown
    footer: Asset Hierarchy
    icon: {fileID: 0}
  - title: Send to Breaker
    message: Defines a Breaker fragment using this prefab. To inspect assets in the
      Prefab Breaker, use drag and drop.
    footer: Asset Hierarchy
    icon: {fileID: 0}
  - title: Show All Prefabs
    message: Hide prefabs marked hidden and blacklisted. Favorited prefabs will still
      be shown
    footer: Asset Hierarchy
    icon: {fileID: 0}
  - title: Hide Prefab
    message: Hide this prefab from the inspector when Show All is disabled
    footer: Asset Hierarchy
    icon: {fileID: 0}
  - title: Blacklist Prefab
    message: Blacklisted prefabs will give a prompt for their removal on map save.
      These prefabs may halt server startup.
    footer: Asset Hierarchy
    icon: {fileID: 0}
  - title: Width
    message: This determins the width of the path and its "Inner" section
    footer: Paths
    icon: {fileID: 0}
  - title: Inner Padding
    message: This is interior area padding each side of the road which remains unaffected
      by Apply Terrain
    footer: Paths
    icon: {fileID: 0}
  - title: Inner Fade
    message: The size of the transition between the Inner Pad and the Inner Depth
    footer: Paths
    icon: {fileID: 0}
  - title: Inner Depth
    message: This is the depth which will be removed from the middle of the path.
      (Set to zero except when creating Rivers)
    footer: Paths
    icon: {fileID: 0}
  - title: Outer Padding
    message: The area on each side of the road which will be set to the same height
      as the road
    footer: Paths
    icon: {fileID: 0}
  - title: Outer Fade
    message: This is the area on each side where the Outer Pad blends with the terrain
    footer: Paths
    icon: {fileID: 0}
  - title: Splat
    message: The selected splat is painted under the path with Apply Terrain
    footer: Paths
    icon: {fileID: 0}
  - title: Topology
    message: The selected topology is painted under the path with Apply Terrain
    footer: Paths
    icon: {fileID: 0}
  - title: Path type
    message: Path type can only be selected before path creation.
    footer: Paths
    icon: {fileID: 0}
  - title: Apply Layers
    message: Modify the terrain to match the path
    footer: Paths
    icon: {fileID: 0}
  - title: Outer Topology
    message: Selected topology will be placed on each side of the Road
    footer: Paths
    icon: {fileID: 0}
  - title: Outer Topology Width
    message: The width of applied Outer Topology
    footer: Paths
    icon: {fileID: 0}
  - title: Generate
    message: Automatically connect beginning and end of path (Only active when path
      has two nodes)
    footer: Paths
    icon: {fileID: 0}
  - title: Density
    message: Increase or decrease the amount of nodes created in automatic pathfinding
    footer: Paths
    icon: {fileID: 0}
  - title: Contour
    message: Increase or decrease the ease of pathfinding over hills
    footer: Paths
    icon: {fileID: 0}
  - title: Terrains
    message: Applies terrain layers associated with monuments and decor. Only enabled
      when selected prefabs contain terrain data
    footer: Inspector
    icon: {fileID: 0}
  - title: Frequency
    message: Removes more spawns as value is increased
    footer: Geology
    icon: {fileID: 0}
  - title: Topological Ranges
    message: When toggle is enabled, constrains spawn within the defined ranges
    footer: Geology
    icon: {fileID: 0}
  - title: Apply Terrains
    message: Automatically applies terrain layers associated with monuments and decor.
      Only enabled when spawned prefabs contain terrain data
    footer: Geology
    icon: {fileID: 0}
  - title: Anchor Jitter
    message: Relocate the anchor point for the geology item within ranges defined
      here
    footer: Geology
    icon: {fileID: 0}
  - title: Preview
    message: Enables and disables spawn preview overlays
    footer: Geology
    icon: {fileID: 0}
  - title: Snap to ocean
    message: When enabled, spawned items will snap to the ocean
    footer: Geology
    icon: {fileID: 0}
  - title: Sorting
    message: These toggles sort spawn orders. Used to help bias spawns when colliders
      are active
    footer: Geology
    icon: {fileID: 0}
  - title: Scale Ranges
    message: Items will receive scale sizes between these ranges
    footer: Geology
    icon: {fileID: 0}
  - title: Lock to X
    message: All scale ranges will match those for X
    footer: Geology
    icon: {fileID: 0}
  - title: Lock Aspect
    message: Randomly chosen scales will always have matching x,y, and z values.
    footer: Geology
    icon: {fileID: 0}
  - title: Terrain Slide
    message: Spawned items will slide along the terrain's surface between the defined
      ranges
    footer: Geology
    icon: {fileID: 0}
  - title: Rotation Ranges
    message: Geology Items spawn with rotations between these ranges
    footer: Geology
    icon: {fileID: 0}
  - title: Snap to Terrain
    message: A Geology Item's base rotation can be aligned to each axis by enabling
      toggles
    footer: Geology
    icon: {fileID: 0}
  - title: Item Flip
    message: Every other item will spawn flipped upside down
    footer: Geology
    icon: {fileID: 0}
  - title: Geology Field
    message: This simulates geological processes with random rotation gradients
    footer: Geology
    icon: {fileID: 0}
  - title: Geology Items
    message: To add items to the list, drag and drop them from the Asset Hierarchy.
      Weight indicates liikelihood to spawn relative to other items.
    footer: Geology
    icon: {fileID: 0}
